// endpoint_update_production_pause.proto — UpdateProductionPause: pause or
// resume ONE REPOSITORY's production checks
// (repoconfig.v1.LifecycleConfig.production_checks). RUNTIME section.
// `agent-repld production-mediation pause|resume -repository here|DIR` asks
// it, and so does the topbar's production-checks chip
// (frontend.v1.TopbarProductionChecks) on a click.
//
// THE PAUSE IS THE DAEMON'S, KEPT PER REPOSITORY. DURABLE: it survives a
// daemon restart and a handover until it is resumed.
//
// PAUSING STOPS THE PRODUCTION MEDIATOR AT ONCE. The mediator's running turn
// is interrupted, a span brief still waiting in its prompt queue is retired
// unsent, and every span owed and not yet decided is dropped: none of them is
// ever reviewed. While the pause stands the daemon tells the mediator no
// span, refuses its decisions and folds (UpdateProductionMediationError
// .paused), and opens every prompt that reaches it with a note saying
// production mediation is paused, so it dispatches nothing and does not work
// around the pause. Its open children are untouched: each lands or closes as
// it would.
//
// RESUMING STARTS THE CHECKS AGAIN AT THE FIRST LANDING AFTER IT. A span that
// ends during the pause is never reviewed, and neither is the one the first
// landing after the resume closes, since it began during the pause: the first
// span told after a resume runs from that landing to the next.

